  "prompt": "**Role**: You are a senior git workflow specialist and technical communication expert with expertise in conventional commits, semantic versioning, git best practices, and commit message optimization. Use the conventional commit types defined below to generate clear, informative commit messages that follow best practices.\n\n**Task**: Generate a professional conventional commit message that clearly\ncommunicates the changes, follows best practices, and provides useful\ncontext for code reviewers and future maintainers.\n\n**Conventional Commit Types:**\n- feat: New feature or capability\n- fix: Bug fix\n- docs: Documentation only changes\n- style: Formatting, whitespace, no code change\n- refactor: Code restructuring without behavior change\n- test: Adding or updating tests\n- chore: Maintenance tasks, tooling, dependencies\n- perf: Performance improvement\n- ci: CI/CD pipeline changes\n\n\n**Context:**\n- Project: bessa_patterns.ts (Library of Reusable Design Patterns in TypeScript)\n- Workflow: Tests & Documentation Automation v0.12.0-alpha\n- Change Scope: feat(implementation+tests): 29 files changed (docs: 8, tests: 4, code: 3, config: 8)\n\n**Git Repository Analysis:**\na51a052 chore(workflow): update docs and metrics and logs and summaries [skip ci]\nc7a5c4e feat(implementation+tests): update docs, tests, and config for workflow automation\naaa145e feat: add Observer pattern tests and API documentation\nb7aeff3 feat: add ObserverSubject and DualObserverSubject\n6baaa97 Initial commit\n\n**Changed Files:**\ngithub/copilot-instructions.md\n.github/workflows/ci.yml\n.workflow-config.yaml\nREADME.md\neslint.config.mjs\njest.config.json\npackage-lock.json\npackage.json\nsrc/DualObserverSubject.ts\nsrc/ObserverSubject.ts\nsrc/index.ts\ntest/DualObserverSubject.test.ts\ntest/ObserverSubject.test.ts\ntest/index.test.ts\ntsconfig.json\n.editorconfig\n.github/dependabot.yml\n.husky/\n.nvmrc\n.prettierrc\nCHANGELOG.md\nCONTRIBUTING.md\ndocs/API.md\ndocs/ARCHITECTURE.md\ndocs/GETTING_STARTED.md\ndocs/README.md\ntest/integration.test.ts\n\n**Staged Commit Statistics (includes workflow artifacts):**\n91 files changed, 13311 insertions(+), 729 deletions(-) (29 project files + workflow artifacts)\n\n**Detailed Context:**\nfeat(implementation+tests): update tests and documentation\nWorkflow automation completed comprehensive validation and updates.\n\nChanges:\n- Modified files: 15\n- Documentation: 8 files\n- Tests: 4 files\n- Scripts: 0 files\n- Code: 3 files\n\nTotal changes: 29 files\n[workflow-automation v0.12.0-alpha]\n\n**Diff Sample (first 100 lines):**\ndiff --git a/.editorconfig b/.editorconfig\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..5428fc3\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.editorconfig\n@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@\n+root = true\n+\n+[*]\n+charset = utf-8\n+end_of_line = lf\n+insert_final_newline = true\n+trim_trailing_whitespace = true\n+\n+[*.{ts,js,json,yaml,yml}]\n+indent_style = space\n+indent_size = 2\n+\n+[*.md]\n+indent_style = space\n+indent_size = 4\n+trim_trailing_whitespace = true\n+insert_final_newline = true\ndiff --git a/.github/dependabot.yml b/.github/dependabot.yml\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..b665139\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.github/dependabot.yml\n@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\n+version: 2\n+updates:\n+  - package-ecosystem: npm\n+    directory: /\n+    schedule:\n+      interval: weekly\n+    open-pull-requests-limit: 5\n+    labels:\n+      - dependencies\ndiff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml\nindex 2f84f8f..14eaed2 100644\n--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml\n+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml\n@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ on:\n   pull_request:\n     branches: [main]\n \n+# Ensures only one workflow run per branch; cancels any in-progress run on new push\n concurrency:\n   group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n   cancel-in-progress: true\n@@ -37,7 +38,7 @@ jobs:\n         run: npm run lint\n \n       - name: Test\n-        run: npm test\n+        run: npm run test:coverage\n \n       - name: Build\n         run: npm run build\ndiff --git a/.husky/pre-commit b/.husky/pre-commit\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..fcaddb4\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.husky/pre-commit\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+npm run lint && npm test\ndiff --git a/.nvmrc b/.nvmrc\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..209e3ef\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.nvmrc\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+20\ndiff --git a/.prettierrc b/.prettierrc\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..a95cb05\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.prettierrc\n@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@\n+{\n+  \"semi\": true,\n+  \"singleQuote\": true,\n+  \"trailingComma\": \"es5\",\n+  \"printWidth\": 100,\n+  \"tabWidth\": 2\n+}\ndiff --git a/.workflow-config.yaml b/.workflow-config.yaml\nindex a5495bd..8814eb4 100644\n--- a/.workflow-config.yaml\n+++ b/.workflow-config.yaml\n@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@ project:\n   type: typescript-library\n   description: Library of Reusable Design Patterns in TypeScript\n   kind: configuration_library\n-  version: 0.11.1-alpha\n+  version: 0.12.0-alpha\n \n tech_stack:\n   primary_language: typescript\n@@ -56,12 +56,12 @@ workflow:\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n1. **Conventional Commit Message Crafting:**\n   - Select appropriate type from the list above\n   - Define clear scope (e.g., deployment, testing, documentation)\n   - Write concise subject line (<50 chars if possible, max 72)\n   - Follow format: type(scope): subject\n   - Use imperative mood (\"add\" not \"added\" or \"adds\")\n   - Don't end subject with period\n\n2. **Semantic Context Integration:**\n   - Analyze what changed and why\n   - Identify the business value or technical benefit\n   - Connect changes to workflow or project goals\n   - Reference workflow automation context\n   - Note automation tool version\n\n3. **Change Impact Description:**\n   - Describe what was changed (files, features, functionality)\n   - Explain why changes were made\n   - Note any architectural or structural improvements\n   - Highlight test coverage or documentation updates\n   - Mention dependency or quality improvements\n\n4. **Breaking Change Detection:**\n   - Identify any breaking changes (API, behavior, interface)\n   - Flag deprecations or removals\n   - Note migration steps if applicable\n   - Assess backward compatibility\n\n5. **Commit Body & Footer Generation:**\n   - Provide detailed multi-line body if needed\n   - List key changes as bullet points\n   - Include relevant issue/PR references\n   - Add footer metadata (automation info, breaking changes)\n   - Follow 72-character line wrap\n\n\n**Approach**: Review ONLY the staged changes listed above. Write commit messages strictly based on the provided diff content — do not reference files, features, or changes not shown.\n\n**Commit Message Format:**\n\ntype(scope): subject line here\n\nOptional body paragraph explaining what and why, not how.\nWrap at 72 characters per line.\n\n- List key changes as bullet points\n- Each bullet should be clear and actionable\n- Focus on user/developer impact\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: describe any breaking changes\nRefs: #issue-number (if applicable)\n[workflow-automation v0.12.0-alpha]\n\n**Remember**: Output only the commit message text with NO markdown\ncode blocks.\n"
